From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:38:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] fixup port 177472ea: the tier's writer reads an evicted
 image only after v0.2.12's background copies have landed

v0.2.12 has background copies into a parked image's host bytes that our base did not have: STRATA_CKPT_ASYNC (a
checkpoint's GDN state) and upstream's STRATA_PARK_ASYNC / STRATA_PARK_VRAM_MIB (the K/V, SavedConversation::pending).
Their rule is that every reader of those bytes joins first (conversation_checkpoint_join / conversation_park_join, as
the SAVE path does).  The tier's writer thread is such a reader, so the eviction sink joins both before it hands a
spillable image over.  Both joins are no-ops when nothing is in flight; the sink only exists with STRATA_CONV_TIER_DIR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/program/generate.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/program/generate.cpp b/src/program/generate.cpp
index 45924928..fc425daf 100644
--- a/src/program/generate.cpp
+++ b/src/program/generate.cpp
@@ -12404,6 +12404,11 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
                     tier.reset();
                 } else {
                     conversations.set_evict_sink([&tier](strata::core::SavedConversation&& image, bool spill) {
+                        if (spill) {   // the writer reads the image's bytes on its own thread: the background copies
+                                       // (STRATA_CKPT_ASYNC, STRATA_PARK_ASYNC) land first, as before a SAVE
+                            strata::core::conversation_checkpoint_join(nullptr);
+                            strata::core::conversation_park_join();
+                        }
                         tier->evicted(std::move(image), spill);
                     });
                 }
